## 5. Technical Requirements

### 5.1 Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|------------|
| Frontend | React.js, TailwindCSS, DaisyUI |
| Backend | Node.js, Express.js |
| Database | MongoDB |
| Real-time | Socket.io |
| AI Services | OpenAI, Gemini, Groq, Claude |
| Media | Cloudinary |
| Scraping | Apify |
| Deployment | Docker, Kubernetes |

### 5.2 API Requirements
- RESTful API design
- JWT authentication
- Rate limiting (1000 requests/15 min)
- Input validation (Zod schemas)
- CORS support
- API versioning (/api/v1)

### 5.3 Performance Requirements
- API response time: < 200ms
- Real-time message delivery: < 100ms
- Lead generation: < 30 seconds per batch
- Concurrent users: 10,000+
- Uptime: 99.9%

### 5.4 Data Requirements
- Lead data retention: 2 years
- Chat message retention: 1 year
- Analytics data retention: 5 years
- Backup frequency: Daily
- Data encryption: AES-256

---

## 6. User Stories

### 6.1 Lead Generation
```
As a business owner,
I want to automatically generate leads from multiple sources,
So that I can expand my customer base without manual research.

Acceptance Criteria:
- System scrapes Google Maps, Instagram, Facebook, LinkedIn, and classified sites
- Leads are automatically saved to database
- Duplicate detection prevents duplicate entries
- Lead scoring is applied automatically
```

### 6.2 Multi-Channel Communication
```
As a sales representative,
I want to communicate with clients via WhatsApp, email, or web chat,
So that I can reach them on their preferred platform.

Acceptance Criteria:
- Messages are delivered across all channels
- Conversation history is unified
- AI suggests responses based on context
- Voice messages are transcribed automatically
```

### 6.3 AI-Powered Lead Qualification
```
As a marketing manager,
I want leads to be automatically scored and qualified,
So that I can focus on high-value prospects.

Acceptance Criteria:
- AI analyzes lead data and behavior
- Leads are scored 0-100
- Qualified leads are flagged and prioritized
- Recommended actions are provided
```

